Example has   System.out.println (rset.getString ("ENAME")); to get ENAME from cursor
SO map your in type Out type parameter and check refcursor for data and from columname you can get data.</p>

<p>How to pass parameters to Procedures and Functions in PL/SQL?
In PL/SQL, we can pass parameters to procedures and functions in three ways.</p>

<p>1) IN type parameter: These types of parameters are used to send values to stored procedures. 
2) OUT type parameter: These types of parameters are used to get values from stored procedures. This is similar to a return type in functions.
3) IN OUT parameter: These types of parameters are used to send values and get values from stored procedures.</p>

